{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1404125-help-with-character-concept","id":1404125,"title":"Help with character concept!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-22T17:22:07-07:00","id":1404125,"title":"Help with character concept!","content":"Hi! I'm new here on the forums, even though I've read a lot here, so I really want to be part of this community and hear your opinions!<br /> So, as stated on the title, I'll be playing in a crossover chronicle and am intent on making a Changeling character.<br /> Our primary restrictions were: No Mages and no Wraiths since no one really knows their system right. At first we would be using only the core book of the revised editions (or for CtD, the second one, and Demon really don't have this problem), but the storyteller said that we will be using the 20th year anniversary instead. <br /> After all is said and done, I was looking for the splats, and found changeling. I've read most of the 20th year book, and decided on some concepts and ideas for my character. But, I'm having some problems with how to make some stuff, and a few problems with some rules, and was hoping you could help me.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of making an Unseelie Wilder Arcadian Sidhe. In concept, he will be opposed to the current rule of the faes, as he believes that a big part of all the problemas we face are the Seelie ruling fault. Since they refuse to leave the power and share it with the Unseelie, it created an imbalance in the Dreaming, and that's why this Autumn has been so bad. The Unseelie need to rule through the Autumn, let the Winter come, and only them a new Spring will be born. After we are back to the Spring, the rule should be divided between factions during the year again.<br /> Now, with the problemas: How do I make an Unseelie character without being a complete A**hole? The Unseelie legacies are so bad. Most have a ban that forces you to be a complete pain, or just borderly unplayable (like, never smile, for example. Had a character who sacrificed his emotions once, it was really unfun and hard to play). Being Seelie is not an option, not only for the concept, as for the fact that I really don't like them very much. They look like self-righteous pricks, and I love much more the concept of personal freedom. The book keeps saying the Unseelie are not evil, then makes the rules force you to be detestable, and all examples of Unseelie I remember now are of traitorous backstabbers.<br /> About being Sidhe: I had the idea that my character was kind of a &quot;new&quot; soul. He would have been born in Arcadia during the Interregnum, and not long (at least in Fae terms) after that, he would've come to the Autumn world. I know the Ressurgence was not and isolated event, but could a Sidhe &quot;return&quot; (even though he was never here in the first place) during the early 90s? My idea is for him to be on his late 20s, early 30s in age, and the idea of being a new soul the reason he doesn't care much about traditions. He probably took the changeling way as soon as he arrived (or the Sidhe way of the latecomers, if I'm not mistaking it was not exactly the Changeling way, but they also took unborn childs, or am I wrong?).In a lesser note: can a Sidhes mien skin be colored? In the same way that trolls are blue or knockers have the red marks on their faces, coul a Sidhe be, for example, purple, dark blue, or anything like? Would that be too weird?<br /> I am really having trouble with choosing a House. I really want to be from an Unseelie house, and I guess house Ailil woud be a natural feat, but my last character in WtA was a Homid Shadow Lord Ragabash. and I'm trying to avoid to many comparison or just end up with someone too similar...<br /> Finally, my biggest mechanical concern. This is will be a crossover chronicle. And knowing my storyteller, it will be a combat heavy one. It will be possible to avoid many combat situations trough guile and dialogue, but eventually it WILL happen. And in a world were a Garou's claws can do aggravated damage, how can any changeling survive an encounter? I mean, the prodigal powers don't affect their chimerical sides, it affects the physical ones. I'm afraid I would be too fragile, in comparison with the other players, even if I had, for example, 5 in stamina (which I probably won't. I intend on being a knight like character in a way, but probably no Physical as my focus).<br /> <br /> About the chronicle: my friend who's the storyteller wants to make all of the players needing to cooperate in the beggining, but to let us choose our own ways as the story goes. Having played a lot with them before (mostly WtA and some VtM, with the eventual crossover), I know our allegiances will be shifitng a lot, even between players. It will be a huge group, and right now, what is expected in the group is 3 demons (don't know much about them. If I'm not mistaken, it will be a Rabisu, Neberu and a Namaru. May be wrong) who'll be independent of each other. A couple of friends will be making a connected backstory. On of them will be a Garou (Fianna Galliard.And knowing my friend, he will either be a metis or a lupus), and his wife will be a Troll, with some kind of oath between them. They are probably making their characters with the intent of being complementary in combat with each other. Another friend of mine wants to make a changeling, but still don't know which kith. His idea of human life before the chrysallis is a kid who is a champion of (or just very competitive) game player (no game yet chosen, probably some MOBA or FPS).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T18:43:17-07:00","id":1404151,"title":"","content":"My recommendation is to find a counterpart to your Unseelie Sidhe idea in some other medium, and see how you can translate that into Changeling. I find that much more inspirational than any Changeling material which I find is often... banal. Da dum dum.<br /> <br /> For example, my go-to example of an Unseelie Sidhe would be The Man With the Thistledown Hair in Jonathon Strange &amp; Mr. Norrell. If you like that, see how you can translate it into Changeling (along with whatever modifications you want to make) mechanics. It shouldn't be a direct translation. But you can probably get a lot of inspiration from it. Other possible inspirations might be Nuada, Crown Prince of the Bethmoora clan in Hellboy II. Or Jade the White Witch of Narnia. There's also various folklore and fairy tales that have a fairy king abducting mortal women, or tricking mortals in malicious ways. There's also a lot of deadly fairy seductresses out there which map to female unseelie sidhe, and you can come up with a male counterpart.<br /> <br /> Usually &quot;Unseelie&quot; type fairies harm mortals because of they violate certain taboos, or act in an immoral way. But they themselves don't bother to act morally. It's very similar to how the Greek gods acted. They routinely punished mortals for things they would do themselves. The rules don't apply to them; but they do enforce them. So that route may be another inspiration in how to act.<br /> <br /> It may not map to the published Unseelie Legacies, but if you have a good idea for one yourself based on that, you can always ask the ST to approve one.<br /> <br /> If you are looking to survive lots of aggravated damage, look at Treasures for a Background and talk with your ST about ideas. A shield or other magical device might give you additional soak dice for aggravated, or allow healing of them. Pick appropriate Realms for any Arts. And look at the rule for invoking the Dragon's Ire.<br /> <br /> The main rule in any crossover, is that supernaturals should never fight fair. Meaning fighting on the home ground of someone else. They should always use powers and tactics that are appropriate for them. Asymmetrical warfare. So you may not want to straight out fight at times. You may want to wait for more fortuitous circumstances. When that happens and other party members intend to fight, you may want to have other powers that can be useful so you can do something while avoiding a combat that may not play to your strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T15:03:13-07:00","id":1404309,"title":"","content":"Hey, first of all, thanks for the replie!<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with The Man With the Thistledown Hair, will be looking on it. On the other hand, very familiar with Nuada and the White Witch, and other fairy tales. But that's not the problem I'm having. I want to make a character that doesn't feel like a caricature of a villain. And that's all the Unseelie looks like from the books. It's not even about morality or being selfish. It's just plain evil. Not even a different set of morality, like an orange/blue allignment.<br /> <br /> Don't know if you are familliar with Magic the Gathering and the color pie. But for example, there's a character who a &quot;Black mana&quot; character, who even though is very selfish, he's still a protagonist who's not straight up evil.<br /> <br /> I guess that's the point. I want to be ambitious, I want to have no qualms with doing what I think is necessary, but not straight up an evil murderous hypocrite backstabber who can never make a single act of kindness or altruism. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1404125-help-with-character-concept?p=1404151#post1404151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main rule in any crossover, is that supernaturals should never fight fair. Meaning fighting on the home ground of someone else. They should always use powers and tactics that are appropriate for them. Asymmetrical warfare. So you may not want to straight out fight at times. You may want to wait for more fortuitous circumstances. When that happens and other party members intend to fight, you may want to have other powers that can be useful so you can do something while avoiding a combat that may not play to your strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really a very good point, which I haven't thought of. After playing WtA so much, I forgot how it feels to not be a killing machine, even without focusing on that. Didn't want to need itens and treasures to hold my own in a combat, but I guess it will have to be it. Maybe an armor. Between that, invoking the Wyrd and manipualting things to only fight on my terms I guess I will be ok. On the Dragon's Ire, as of the 20th edition, it's now just an Art with 5 levels of cantrips to use with realms (and it's on my list of Arts to get hahaha)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}